286,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.05563543595935805,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":52.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.017645443621139855,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":32.4,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09142396491202326,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.04126638418572148,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.002643057832692577,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":95.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.58856,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.75,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":75.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Delek Logistics Partners, LP provides gathering, pipeline, transportation, and other services for crude oil, intermediates, refined products, natural gas, storage, wholesale marketing, terminalling water disposal and recycling customers in the United States. The company operates in four segments: Gathering and Processing, Wholesale Marketing and Terminalling, Storage and Transportation, and Investments in Joint Ventures. It offers tanks, offloading facilities, and trucks and ancillary assets that provide crude oil, hydrocarbon-based products, intermediate and refined products transportation, and storage services. Delek Logistics GP, LLC serves as the general partner of the company. Delek Logistics Partners, LP was incorporated in 2012 and is headquartered in Brentwood, Tennessee. Delek Logistics Partners, LP operates as a subsidiary of Delek US Holdings, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Avigal  Soreq CPA | President, CEO & Chairman of Delek Logistics GP, LLC | Age 47","financial_summary":["Delek Logistics Partners, L.P. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.0B market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","The company is burning through $31M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 59% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 85% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8452316113429749},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 62/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (75% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Delek Logistics Partners (DKL) Declares Q3 Distribution Following A Fairly Priced Valuation View","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-dkl/delek-logistics-partners/news/delek-logistics-partners-dkl-declares-q3-distribution-follow","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794009120.781,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Delek Logistics (DKL) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/delek-logistics-dkl-q3-2026-234440000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794008962.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Delek Logistics raises 2026 adjusted EBITDA guidance to $530M-$560M as sour gas system nears startup (NYSE:DKL)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668622-delek-logistics-raises-2026-adjusted-ebitda-guidance-to-530m-560m-as-sour-gas-system-nears","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000423.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"c